1. Reference to Pending Application
This notice concerns application PXA-2024-0161, on file with Alleniom Utilities' DER Interconnection
Program and currently held in the on-hold queue pending receipt of customer-provided information previously
requested by Interconnection Studies. The Company's outstanding request for information — most recently
reiterated by written correspondence from Interconnection Studies to the applicant of record — has not received
a substantive response. Absent such a response, the application cannot be advanced through technical screening.
2. Tariff Basis
Pursuant to Alleniom's APUC-filed tariff §12.4, this Notice of Impending Withdrawal/Cancellation is hereby
served. If Alleniom Utilities does not receive a substantive response within 30 business days of the date of this
notice, the application shall be deemed withdrawn.
3. Business-Day Convention
For purposes of the response window established under §12.4, "business days" exclude Saturdays, Sundays, and
federal legal public holidays observed within the response period. Federal holidays falling within any portion of
the response window shall not be counted toward the 30-business-day period.
4. Response Deadline
The applicable response deadline shall be computed by adding thirty (30) business days to the date of this
notice, applying the business-day convention set out in §3 above. The applicant is responsible for computing the
applicable deadline from the date shown at the top of this notice.
5. Required Response
A substantive response consists of a written submission, addressed to Interconnection Studies at the address
shown in the letterhead or by email to der.program@alleniom.com, that materially addresses the outstanding
information request associated with PXA-2024-0161. The Company will treat the postmark date (for mailed
submissions) or the timestamp of receipt (for electronic submissions) as the date of response.

6. Consequence of Non-Response
Failure to submit a substantive response within the period stated in §2 above shall result in application
PXA-2024-0161 being deemed withdrawn and closed from the active queue without further action of the
Company, in accordance with §12.4. A subsequent DER interconnection request for the same site would require
submission of a new application, which would take its own queue position as of the date determined complete.
7. Contact
Questions concerning the outstanding information request or the procedural effect of this notice may be directed
to Interconnection Studies at der.program@alleniom.com or (612) 555-0100.
